<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  THE SAME REFUSAL AS res/xml/data_extraction_rules.xml, IN THE FORMAT
  ANDROID 11 AND LOWER UNDERSTANDS.

  minSdkVersion here is 24 and targetSdkVersion is 36, so this app runs
  across both backup configuration formats. Android's Auto Backup guide
  keeps them strictly separate:

      "Use the following XML syntax for the configuration file that
       controls backup for devices running Android 11 or lower."
       <full-backup-content> ... </full-backup-content>

      "Important: Even if your app targets Android 12 or higher, you must
       also specify another set of XML backup rules to support devices
       that run Android 11 (API level 30) or lower."

  Android Lint said the same thing about the manifest as it stood:

      DataExtractionRules  AndroidManifest.xml:15
      The attribute `android:dataExtractionRules` only applies for
      Android 12 and higher; since `minSdkVersion` is API 24 you should
      also set `android:fullBackupContent`

  This file is that second set of rules. It is the answer to the warning,
  not a suppression of it: nothing about the finding is being silenced,
  the missing half is being written.

  This is defence in depth, and the depth is deliberate. On API 24-30 the
  primary control is still android:allowBackup="false", which on those
  releases does disable Auto Backup outright - the "varies by
  manufacturer" caveat in Android's guide is scoped to apps targeting
  API 31 and above. If allowBackup is ever flipped, on purpose or by a
  merged library manifest, this file is what decides the answer, and the
  answer it gives is the same as everywhere else: nothing.

  Every domain the API 30 schema defines, excluded at path="." - the
  spelling the guide's own examples use for a whole domain.
-->
<full-backup-content>
    <exclude domain="root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="." />
    <exclude domain="external" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_root" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_file" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_database" path="." />
    <exclude domain="device_sharedpref" path="." />
</full-backup-content>
